{"Title":"An Act relative to penalties for crimes against seniors ","BillNumber":"H1531","DocketNumber":"HD2945","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"C_G1","Name":"Carlos González","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/C_G1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T14:04:15.97"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"C_G1","Name":"Carlos González","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/C_G1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T14:04:15.97"},{"Id":"BMA1","Name":"Brian M. Ashe","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BMA1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-30T20:00:10.56"},{"Id":"V_H1","Name":"Vanna Howard","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/V_H1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-31T12:35:41.4933333"},{"Id":"BLW1","Name":"Bud L. Williams","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BLW1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T15:35:30.9066667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1531/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative González of Springfield, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1531) of Carlos González and others relative to penalties for crimes against seniors.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSection 13K of chapter 265 of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by adding the following subsection:- \r\n\t(g) Whenever any person has been convicted of subsections (a½) to (e), inclusive, when the victim of such crime is an elder or a person residing in senior housing, the person convicted shall register annually for 5 consecutive years with the office of probation, which shall maintain a central registry of all such persons. The registration shall include (i) the offender’s home address and any secondary addresses; (ii) the offender’s work address; (iii) the offender’s age, sex, race, height, weight, eye and hair color; (iv) a photograph of the offender; and (v) whether the offender is in compliance with the registration requirement of this subsection. Whoever fails to register as required by this subsection shall be punished by imprisonment in the house of correction for not more than 2½ years, or by a fine of not more than $5,000, or by both such fine and imprisonment. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}